#General Quality Controls

option.BaseQuality=Base Quality
value.BaseQuality.0 = Low
value.BaseQuality.1 = Mid
value.BaseQuality.2 = High
option.BaseQuality.comment=Reduce the ammount of texture blurring samples, heavier math functions, and performance slow downs.  Below options denote fidelity, this option is how that fidelity is utilized.  Note - Color blindness math is estimated on Low & Mid levels for performance, if an issue, contact me.

# -- -- --

#Color Values & Gamma

option.LightBlackLevel=Dark Color Levels
option.LightBlackLevel.comment=Set how dark lighting can get; This offsets darker color values to brighten the entire environment. Lower values are moodier, higher values are better for streaming or video recording. 0.0, blacks = §8black. 0.5, blacks = §7grey. 1.0, blacks = white 

option.LightWhiteLevel=Bright Color Levels
option.LightWhiteLevel.comment=Set how bright block lighting can get. As light emitting blocks also appear to glow, this will also affect how much glow is visible.  0.0, white = §7grey. 1.0, white = white. 2.0, white = §l§oBLINDING

option.FogAmount=Fog Amount
option.FogAmount.comment=Set how much the fog influences the world.

# -- -- --

#Screen Style Effects

option.GlowBrightness=Glow Amount
option.GlowBrightness.comment=Set how bright glow appears. Glow from light emitting blocks, along with brighter colored blocks in direct sunlight / near lighting (torches, lanterns, etc), and particles. 0.0, no glow. 1.0, default glow. 2.0, blown out glow colors.

option.DetailBlurring=Detail Blurring
option.DetailBlurring.comment=Set ammount of texture blending of blocks, entities, etc.  Detail Blurring works with custom resource packs. 0.0, no detail blurring. 1.0, default blurring. 2.0, blocks appear a solid color.

option.EdgeShading=Edge Outlines
option.EdgeShading.comment=Visibility of Edges in game, appearing lighter Overworld, darker in the Nether.  0.0, no visible edges. 1.0, default edges (slightly transparent, ~2px wide). 2.0, overdrive edges (100% visible, ~4px wide)

# -- -- --

#Environment Effects

option.UnderWaterBlur=Under Water Effects
option.UnderWaterBlur.comment=Toggle Blurring & Warping while under water. If you get dizzy or sick under water, turn this False

option.SolidLeaves=Solid Leaves
option.SolidLeaves.comment=Toggle Solid Leaf Colors.  True, to match Mojang's promo/key art style. False, leaves will appear as default, see through leaves.

# -- -- --

#Shadow Options

option.shadowMapResolution=Shadow Resolution
value.shadowMapResolution.16384=16384§c§6(!)
option.shadowMapResolution.comment=Size of the texture generated for shadows. 512, low quality, better performance. 4096, high quality, slower performance. 16384, §oonly use for high quality video, fps may drop.

option.ShadowSampleCount=Shadow Quality
value.ShadowSampleCount.0=Off
value.ShadowSampleCount.1=Low
value.ShadowSampleCount.2=Mid
value.ShadowSampleCount.3=High
value.ShadowSampleCount.4=Best
option.ShadowSampleCount.comment=Set the quality of shadows. Off, no shadows. Low, simple shadows, 1 sample.  Mid, mellow shadows, 5 samples. High, goose down pillow soft shadows, 9 samples.

# -- -- --

#Debugging Effects
option.DebugView=Debug Vision
value.DebugView.0=Off
value.DebugView.1=Detail Blurring
value.DebugView.2=Shadow Cam
value.DebugView.3=Shadow Debug
value.DebugView.4=Vanilla vs procPromo
option.DebugView.comment=Toggle Debugging Colors & Effects; used in development of this shader pack. Detail Blurring, test blurring methods and side-by-side views.  Shadow Cam, see what the sun & moon see.  Shadow Debug, shadow sample positions. Vanilla vs procPromo, side-by-side comparison

